  "worked_solution": "We start by sketching the solutions to the two inequalities separately:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/468dea33da7365430c2e08bcbf13d176fdafabf64aaac0a940a01c108b1b0e64.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/413c2bbe7a61c8983ea92ff4bb73bba27fc05856eae5f1fdb9614aa2b50f92aa.png)\n\nThe common set of values consists of the values that are in both intervals. So, it can be graphed by finding where the two intervals overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/51a4f2d24dd17ae11e1530b6765782163b9c8f79b69509b458037e747ae0dd37.png)\n\nTherefore, the common set of values is\n$(3,5].$",
