  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-102006\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>We start by sketching the solutions to the two inequalities separately:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-102006-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-102006-e-0\"></div>\n\n\n\n<div id=\"graphic-q-102006-e-1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-102006-e-1\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p>The common set of values consists of the values that are in both intervals. So, it can be graphed by finding where the two intervals overlap:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-102006-e-2\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-102006-e-2\"></div>\n\n<p>Therefore, the common set of values is\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"22\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mstyle></mrow><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</div>",
